{"availability":"available","full":"SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW","name":"NLR-PSM3-2-EPW","description":"Convert NREL PSM3 / NSRDB solar data into EnergyPlus Weather (EPW) files — Streamlit web app and Python tool for building energy simulation.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":2,"created":"2021-02-10T06:35:25Z","updated":"2026-10-07T17:02:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nrel-psm3-2-epw.streamlit.app/","topics":["building-energy","building-energy-simulation","climate","converter","downloader","energyplus","epw","epw-files","nrel","nrel-psm3-data","nsrdb","psm3","python","solar-radiation","streamlit","tmy","weather"],"demo":"https://nrel-psm3-2-epw.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.469Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.469Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.469Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.469Z","stars":1,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["NLR-PSM3-2-EPW is a free, open-source Python tool and Streamlit web app that converts NREL Physical Solar Model (PSM v3.2.2 / v4.0.0, NSRDB) solar and meteorological data into EnergyPlus Weather (EPW) files for building energy simulation. Pick any location by latitude / longitude and download a ready-to-use .epw for a specific year or a Typical Meteorological Year (TMY).","Getting hourly weather data into an EnergyPlus-ready EPW file usually means manual API calls and column wrangling. This tool automates the full NSRDB → EPW pipeline — click a point on a map, choose a year or TMY, and download the weather file.","An EnergyPlus Weather (EPW) file is the standard hourly weather format consumed by EnergyPlus and most building energy simulation engines. It contains a full year (8760 hours) of solar, temperature, humidity, wind and sky-cover data for a single location, and is the starting point for energy modeling, daylighting and thermal-comfort analysis."],"features":["PSM3 / NSRDB → EPW conversion — turns NREL solar climate data into EnergyPlus Weather format.","Interactive map — pick a location by clicking, or enter latitude / longitude manually.","TMY and single-year datasets — download tmy, tgy, tdy, or a specific historical year (≥ 1998).","Resilient downloads — automatically falls back to core attributes when a dataset is","sparse at a location, so remote points still produce a valid EPW."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1673a43360cc620db8906268fc745a8b81662eaff3e8e9d75ffb9ace7df2358d","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.585Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.585Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"NLR-PSM3-2-EPW is a free, open-source Python tool and Streamlit web app that converts NREL Physical Solar Model (PSM v3.2.2 / v4.0.0, NSRDB) solar and meteorological data into EnergyPlus Weather (EPW) files for building energy simulation. Pick any location by latitude / longitude and download a ready-to-use .epw for a specific year or a Typical Meteorological Year (TMY).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Configure your API key:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1673a43360cc620db8906268fc745a8b81662eaff3e8e9d75ffb9ace7df2358d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.585Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T17:02:20Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SustainableUrbanSystemsLab/NLR-PSM3-2-EPW/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:46.585Z","hash":"1673a43360cc620db8906268fc745a8b81662eaff3e8e9d75ffb9ace7df2358d","originalBytes":4343,"